# CQ 29: Which AI systems state a controllability, and what does it allow?
#
# 3.5.6 defines controllability as the property of an AI system that allows a
# human or another external agent to intervene in its functioning.
#
# The entry that matters most for an AI system inside an automated plant, since
# it says whether the plant can take over. Recorded as a relation to a thing
# rather than as a value, because what matters is what the intervention
# consists of.
PREFIX iso:  <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#>
PREFIX inst: <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989/instances#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
SELECT ?system ?controllability
WHERE { ?system iso:hasControllability ?controllability }
ORDER BY ?system
